// token; on the non-EOS path, AppendConstrainedToken preserves validity.
// progress: Each recursive non-base branch decreases maxSteps by at least one
// and adds exactly the token budget consumed locally to the returned cost. The
// open and close branches consume one token-step and append at most one visible
// delimiter. The repair branch consumes one token-step while rollback can only
// shrink or preserve visible output, so the output-length bound is preserved.
// The symbol branch consumes stepsUsed token-steps and ConstrainedSymbolInGenerated
// appends at most that much visible output, even if some consumed tokens are
// rejected suffix tokens or EOS. The token-step branch consumes one token-step;
// EOS may add no visible token, and non-EOS appends exactly one token via
// AppendConstrainedToken. Therefore |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + maxSteps
// and cost <= maxSteps are preserved by induction.
// CSD_PROOF_SKETCH_END
